# Security And Credentials

- Follow `AGENTS.md`; default to least privilege and explicit tenant checks.
- Never print, expose, commit, or move real secrets, portal credentials, encrypted credential payloads, tokens, signed URLs, storage state, or private keys.
- `CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `INTERNAL_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, ePN, Proof, DocuSign, Twilio, Stripe, and captcha secrets are server/worker only.
- Credential encryption lives in `lib/crypto/credential-encryption.js`; credential retrieval/listing lives in `lib/credentials/*`. Human review is required for changes.
- Service-role operations must be protected by auth/role checks and tenant scope. RLS must not be weakened or bypassed to make a feature work.
- Do not return decrypted passwords to clients. Admin/contractor credential APIs should return metadata and masked values only.
- Do not modify payment, notarization, e-recording, legal document, or permit finalization behavior without identifying security/financial/legal impact.
- Review diffs for accidental secret additions before finishing.
